+**ASTRA-SC1 cycle 3 — SF4 verification pass**
+
+**CLOSED: all six requested findings are FIXED. L1r releases actually recomposed under `sf4-release-v1` are usable for wave 1c as a pseudo-label experiment.** This is the requested verification of the existing witnesses, not a new review cycle or an expansion of scope.
+
+Verified on 17 October 2026 in `/Users/foivoskarounos-zamparloukos/Projects/greek-ocr-toolkit-spellcheck`, branch `opus/spellcheck`, HEAD **`47f7b6b0f141e21949be4d12e37333b71f3d37f0`**. The current policy binding is **`sf4-release-v1`**, SHA-256 **`52fb3a5b183b214f6fe1e0986672060b4b41493b9a731ffa259c022714184a36`**, matching SF4's declared binding. [Replay receipt and policy-source hashes](ASTRA-SC1c3v_evidence/scoped_replay_receipt.json). Source references below are relative to the repository root.
+
+| Finding | Verdict | Current probe output and repair evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| **C3-B01 — capital overhead-diaeresis clipping bypass** | **FIXED** | Both saved **Ϊ→Ι** and **Ϋ→Υ** witnesses now return `status: hold`, reason **`detector_clipped_top`**, and **no released `label` field**. Their stored SF3 outcomes were `corrected`. The unchanged geometry tests also pass: two overhead fragments touch the top border and the real geometry helper records `clipped_top=True`. SF4 removes the capital side-zone exception: `greekocr/labelfix/release_gate.py:169–191`; the cut veto is applied at `:225–230`. [Saved-input replay](ASTRA-SC1c3v_evidence/capital_saved.json). |
+| **C3-M01 — owner-page evidence envelope** | **FIXED** | On the original `ι`, A=B=empty, E=`subscript`, bottom-clipped witness, **runtime = complete-envelope page = HOLD / `detector_clipped_bottom`**. Text, every serialized slot and `evidence_sha256` match exactly. The original partial page call also now HOLDs; its reasons are `r1_B_missing`, `r1_B_missing_coverage`, `K1:flag`. This partial-call result alone is not the parity proof: the full-envelope replay supplies that proof. `release_gate.py:340–379` binds all peer evidence and consumes diagnostic E; `scripts/labelfix/owner_pages_build_combined.py:164–196` loads bound runtimes, checks page inputs, delegates to that composer and vetoes legacy partial calls. [Page/runtime output](ASTRA-SC1c3v_evidence/ensemble_page.json). |
+| **C3-N01 — U+02BC alias abort** | **FIXED** | The original historical-slot input **`δʼ` → `δ’`** completes without an exception, with `hold_slots: []`, one letter slot, and the complete former modifier-apostrophe slot retained under `geometry.elision_alias_slots`. `greekocr/labelfix/text.py:36–47` classifies the declared elision aliases consistently; `release_gate.py:262–275` migrates historical alias slots while retaining their records. [Alias output](ASTRA-SC1c3v_evidence/modifier_alias.json). |
+| **C2-N02 residual — unbound notes in implicit-change approval** | **FIXED** | The exact original CLI fixture now raises **`ValueError: notes require --review-binding before approval language`** and creates **no approval output**. `scripts/labelfix/owner_implicit_changes.py:70–80` invokes the shared validator before comparison/output and records the notes/binding hashes. `scripts/labelfix/box_regression.py:116–127` verifies the reviewed page and exact notes bytes. The earlier notes-required/tampering/box-CLI tests pass; the identical-box owner-change probe still reports **one `owner_changed`, zero lost, zero added**. [CLI rejection](ASTRA-SC1c3v_evidence/notes_binding.json), [box replay](ASTRA-SC1c3v_evidence/cycle2_uncertainty_boxes.json). |
+| **C2-B01 — corrections accepted despite recorded uncertainty** | **FIXED** | The original UNKNOWN/no-pixels, UNKNOWN/out-of-image, segmentation and clipped-detector inputs all **HOLD in both PRESENCE and FULL: 8/8**, with no emitted overlay label. The selected repository regressions also pass for missing/unscored coverage, missing predictions, unnamed/localisation uncertainty and recomposition despite cached old decisions. The outstanding capital counterexample is closed by C3-B01 above. Observation decisions are at `release_gate.py:219–256`; recomposition and no-label-on-HOLD are at `scripts/labelfix/clariden/l1_common.py:45–60`. [Uncertainty outputs](ASTRA-SC1c3v_evidence/cycle2_uncertainty_boxes.json), [pytest output](ASTRA-SC1c3v_evidence/pytest_witnesses.log). |
+| **C2-M02 — page/composer parity** | **FIXED** | The same saved owner fixture gives **92/92 exact PRESENCE text/slot/evidence-digest matches**, **15/15 former missing-prediction/localisation/unnamed witnesses HOLD**, and both previously missing opening quotes are restored. The ENSEMBLE_AB diagnostic-E residual is closed by the full-envelope replay above. The shared page entry is `owner_pages_build_combined.py:183–196`; binding/composition is `release_gate.py:340–379`. [92-line output](ASTRA-SC1c3v_evidence/owner92.json). |
+
+**Repository-test confirmation.** The Ϊ→Ι witness is present at `tests/labelfix/test_sf4_review.py:64–72`, parameterized for Ι and Υ. It executes the real geometry helper and the actual L1 overlay, then asserts `status == 'hold'`. Both parameterizations passed. The entire repository test file is **byte-identical** to my original `ASTRA-SC1c3_evidence/test_c3_scope.py`: SHA-256 **`54614ffdcb51f4355bf28c6094ec2a0dd845f2ec7ddbfde39ef8242c8e011582`**. [Identity receipt](ASTRA-SC1c3v_evidence/witness_identity.json). The direct replay additionally checks that no released label accompanies either capital HOLD.
+
+The current pytest run reports **44 passed in 0.82s**: five unchanged original cycle-3 tests, the five identical repository tests, and 34 selected cycle-2 regression cases for these findings. The original cycle-3 review recorded those five witnesses failing on SF3; this pass reran them against the current code. [Full current test output](ASTRA-SC1c3v_evidence/pytest_witnesses.log).
+
+The saved-data checks are implemented in [scoped_replay.py](ASTRA-SC1c3v_evidence/scoped_replay.py), with [execution output](ASTRA-SC1c3v_evidence/scoped_replay.log). The 92-line fixture is the same historical A-only PRESENCE evidence used before. Its existing page, prediction and coverage bindings were checked; its raw detector records were reused. The adapter now passes those inputs through `bind_runtime` and `combine(..., runtime=...)`. No B/E predictions were invented for that fixture. The separate original ensemble witness supplies A/B/E and tests the repaired E-sensitive path. Legacy partial calls are tested separately and abstain.
+
+All pytest execution used the specified Python interpreter, ran from the repository root with `PYTHONPATH` set to that root, and used `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` plus `-p no:cacheprovider`. No network, GPU, CTC/R1 inference or native-crop decoding was performed. The capital pixel witnesses are synthetic arrays. Review files are confined to this writable scratch directory; repository HEAD and status were unchanged at the final check.
+
+**Wave-1c decision: yes for L1r releases recomposed under the verified SF4 policy.** The six defects no longer block the pseudo-label experiment. This decision does not certify a newly published full training-wave payload: that was not part of this verification pass. The previously required source/original-label hashes, kept/control pairing, exclusions, policy/checkpoint bindings and exclusion of every HOLD remain the release contract. Pre-SF4 payloads are not made current by renaming them. Retain the existing verbatim ensemble caveat:
+
+> A and B share training data (C1 agreement labels) and therefore share errors; agreement measures the reader's stability, not an independent pixel signal. Precision on the training waves is unmeasured until the training-wave DEV with print truth exists. Wave 1c on this release is a pseudo-label experiment.
+
+No new finding is raised. The coordinator's deferred R0/R2/S7 work remains outside this verification verdict.
+
+ASTRA-SC1c3v VERDICT: CLOSED; fixed 6/6; L1r releases recomposed under sf4-release-v1 usable for wave 1c as a pseudo-label experiment: yes

